assignee:[reviewer] reviewer (codex)
description:Add a separate minimal Go build skill fixture and generated build-driver vectors that are implementation-neutral. Cover the accepted valid declaration and every security-relevant rejection at the manifest, filesystem, toolchain, dependency graph, compiler directive, process, cache, and context boundaries.
scope:Work in curator-spec after the schema-case generator task. Own a new separate Go fixture below conformance/v1/fixtures, its expected context and identity artifacts, new conformance/v1/vectors/build-drivers.json, and the corresponding generator functions and tests in tools/generate-vectors. Keep the existing script golden fixture and registry hashes unchanged. Include a transitive embedded input and vendored dependency variant. Do not add shared transaction lifecycle scenarios here.
ac:Positive vectors cover schema 6 build_roots, mixed script and build commands, build-source exclusion while unrelated context remains visible, valid vendor-only main packages, all five direct Go argv forms, fixed environment, protected cache hit, compiler-free dry-run miss, and exact CCJ-1 build input, cache key, stored receipt, receipt hash, marker, artifact identity, curator-build-source-v1 bytes, and curator-go-toolchain-v1 bytes; build-source vectors exercise the domain prefix, unsigned UTF-8 ordering, uint64be framing, empty and binary files, root .csk-install.json, mode and timestamp non-inputs, invalid Unicode, duplicate paths, links and special files, mutation during use, and the legacy NUL-stream structural-collision regression; toolchain vectors exercise unsorted files, directories and internal links, LF and CRLF version normalization, mode and timestamp non-inputs, malformed version output, invalid Unicode, duplicate paths, escaping links, a selected executable outside GOROOT, and tree mutation; negative vectors cover schema 5, unknown driver and forbidden fields, missing unused overlapping or runtime-overlapping roots, root or escaped source, links and special files, nested module, non-main or multiple package, missing or inconsistent vendor data, workspace or toolchain switching, unsupported Go family, cgo and native inputs, syso, assembly includes, escaped embed inputs, go:cgo_import_dynamic, generators, PGO, poisoned environment and fake Go, telemetry failure, external-link or libgcc fallback, toolchain path and digest failures, cache key or target or receipt or artifact corruption, noncanonical receipt, concurrent publisher, forged self-consistent receipt outside protected state, and marker-embed build-source regression; cache-hit and dry-run context vectors run no source-aware Go commands; generation is deterministic, go test ./tools/generate-vectors passes, and existing script-fixture and registry expected hashes remain unchanged.
