+# TASK-260720-3ag6pi acceptance and negative-vector coverage
+
+All names below are executable cases in the integrated `curator-spec`
+`1.0.0-rc.4` candidate. `make validate` passed with the validator's exact
+35-schema, 129-schema-case, and 189-manifest-entry inventories; the Go
+generator tests pin the named vector inventories and generated bytes.
+
+## Story acceptance criteria
+
+| STORY-260720-35dck7 acceptance criterion | Passing executable evidence |
+|---|---|
+| A new schema version validates the agreed build declarations. | Schema cases `agent-skill-v6/valid.json`, `csk-skill-v6/valid.json`, `build-receipt-v1/valid.json`, `install-marker-v2/valid.json`, and `conformance-claim-v2/valid.json`; invalid v6 structural cases prove the surface is closed. |
+| Go driver semantics and install ordering are normative. | Build-driver cases `fixed-environment-and-five-direct-argv-forms`, `valid-standard-library-only-main`, and `valid-vendor-only-main-with-transitive-embed`; lifecycle cases `all-source-and-trust-gates-before-build`, `provider-first-and-lexical-command-order`, `deterministic-lock-order`, and `deterministic-target-order-and-consumer-last`. |
+| Build sources are excluded from agent context. | Positive case `build-root-excluded-from-agent-context`; rejection cases `build-root-content-in-context` and `marker-embed-build-source-regression`; `protected-cache-hit` and `compiler-free-dry-run-miss` both contain no source-aware Go command. |
+| Dry-run and audit-before-build are explicit. | Lifecycle `all-source-and-trust-gates-before-build` puts source audit, registry, attestation, and revocation gates before toolchain/cache/build; `compiled-cache-miss-is-read-only`, `project-upgrade`, and `global-upgrade` prohibit persistent effects and source-aware build commands. |
+| Compatibility and security impact are recorded. | Byte-identical legacy schemas/cases for agent-skill and csk-skill v1-v5, install-marker-v1, and conformance-claim-v1; security cases `self-consistent-forged-receipt-outside-protected-state`, `cgo-import-dynamic`, `external-link-required`, and receipt schema cases `invalid-self-asserted-trusted.json`, `invalid-self-asserted-provenance.json`, and `invalid-self-asserted-manager-created.json`. The normative impact is recorded in `COMPATIBILITY.md`, `SECURITY.md`, and decision 0004. |
+| Vectors cover valid builds and all key rejection cases. | Seven `positive_cases`, 75 `rejection_cases`, ten `build_source_cases`, twelve `toolchain_cases`, and the compiled lifecycle groups all passed exact inventory validation. The detailed rejection-cluster mapping follows. |
+| Specification validation and deterministic regeneration pass. | `make validate`, two clean `make regenerate` runs, `make regenerate-check`, and `make release-check VERSION=1.0.0-rc.4` passed. Both regenerated 190-file trees have aggregate SHA-256 `41aa37774478c26377455877ee79ef74f8cb5cf5562ea5b1501e5c94fe9c1fa0`. |
+
+## Minimum rejection clusters
+
+| Rejection cluster | Passing schema cases or vectors |
+|---|---|
+| Structural manifest | `schema-5-build-command`, `unknown-driver`, `forbidden-args`, `forbidden-env`, `forbidden-output`, `forbidden-toolchain`, `forbidden-hooks`, `mixed-script-build-shape`; agent-skill-v6 and csk-skill-v6 cases `invalid-build-missing-driver.json`, `invalid-build-missing-source-dir.json`, `invalid-build-unsupported-driver.json`, `invalid-build-mixed-script.json`, `invalid-build-mixed-system.json`, `invalid-build-args.json`, `invalid-build-env.json`, `invalid-build-flags.json`, `invalid-build-hooks.json`, `invalid-build-output.json`, `invalid-build-scripts.json`, `invalid-build-tags.json`, and `invalid-build-toolchain.json`. |
+| Build-root, source, and context paths | `missing-build-roots`, `missing-build-root-directory`, `unused-build-root`, `overlapping-build-roots`, `runtime-overlapping-build-root`, `root-build-root`, `build-root-symlink`, `build-root-special-file`, `root-source-dir`, `escaped-source-dir`, `source-outside-root`, `source-link`, `source-special-file`, `source-not-directory`, `missing-root-go-mod`, `nested-module`, `non-main-package`, `multiple-packages`, and `build-root-content-in-context`. |
+| Build-source identity algorithm | `invalid-unicode-build-source-path`, `duplicate-build-source-path`, `build-source-symbolic-link`, `build-source-special-file`, `build-source-mutation-during-use`, `root-marker-bytes-are-build-input`, `legacy-nul-stream-structural-collision`, and the rejected `marker-embed-build-source-regression`; positive byte anchors `fixture-exact-build-source`, `domain-prefix-ordering-framing-empty-binary-and-root-marker`, and `mode-and-timestamp-are-non-inputs`. |
+| Toolchain identity and release boundary | `toolchain-version-missing-terminal-lf`, `toolchain-version-multiple-terminal-newlines`, `invalid-unicode-toolchain-path`, `duplicate-toolchain-path`, `escaping-toolchain-link`, `absolute-toolchain-link`, `dangling-toolchain-link`, `selected-go-outside-goroot`, `toolchain-tree-mutation-during-use`, `wrong-go-executable-path`, `toolchain-digest-mismatch`, `unsupported-go-pre-1-23`, and `unsupported-go-future-family`; normalization anchors `unsorted-directories-files-and-internal-link`, `crlf-version-normalizes-to-lf-identity`, and `toolchain-mode-and-timestamp-are-non-inputs`. |
+| Module, dependency, and compiler-input graph | `missing-vendored-dependency`, `inconsistent-vendor-modules`, `workspace-only-dependency`, `toolchain-switch-request`, `cgo-only-package`, `native-c-input`, `native-cxx-input`, `native-swig-input`, `root-syso`, `transitive-syso`, `root-assembly-absolute-include`, `transitive-assembly-escaping-include`, `escaped-embed-input`, `cgo-import-dynamic`, `attempted-go-generate`, and `default-pgo`. |
+| Process and host isolation | `poisoned-path`, `inherited-goflags-toolexec`, `inherited-goenv`, `inherited-gowork`, `vcs-metadata`, `repository-local-fake-go`, `telemetry-command-failure`, `telemetry-private-dir-escape`, `external-link-required`, `libgcc-fallback-attempt`, `child-outside-goroot-tools`, and `wrong-go-executable-path`. The accepted driver case records `shell_used: false` and `artifact_executed: false`. |
+| Cache, receipt, and protected-state trust | `cache-key-mismatch`, `cache-wrong-target`, `cache-wrong-toolchain`, `cache-wrong-policy`, `cache-wrong-build-source`, `receipt-hash-mismatch`, `artifact-hash-mismatch`, `artifact-size-mismatch`, `artifact-path-mismatch`, `noncanonical-receipt-whitespace`, `noncanonical-receipt-trailing-lf`, `partial-cache-entry`, `artifact-link`, `artifact-special-file`, `concurrent-publisher-different-bytes`, and `self-consistent-forged-receipt-outside-protected-state`; build-receipt-v1 invalid cases cover missing inputs/artifacts, algorithm/policy mismatches, physical paths, and self-asserted trust/provenance. |
+| Cache-hit, dry-run, and marker/context regression | `protected-cache-hit`, `compiler-free-dry-run-miss`, `build-root-excluded-from-agent-context`, `marker-embed-build-source-regression`, and `build-root-content-in-context`; lifecycle `compiled-cache-miss-is-read-only` prohibits `go list`, `go build`, and every named persistent mutation. |
+| Claim transition and stale-suite evidence | Conformance-claim-v2 cases `invalid-protocol-version-rc3.json`, `invalid-schema-version-1.json`, `invalid-duplicate-classes.json`, `invalid-result-fail.json`, and `invalid-unknown-field.json`; release-gate tests `test_rejects_claim_v1_redefined_for_rc4`, `test_rejects_rc3_suite_hash_as_rc4_evidence`, and `test_rejects_duplicate_suite_hash_in_rc4_claim`. Frozen claim-v1 remains rc.3 byte-for-byte. |
+| Private build failure and cache publication | Lifecycle `all-misses-stage-and-verify-before-home-lock`, `second-build-failure-preserves-persistent-state`, `publish-complete-immutable-entry-under-home-lock`, `concurrent-identical-winner`, `concurrent-determinism-mismatch`, `corrupt-live-entry`, and `untrusted-cache-boundary`. |
+| Commit, target-swap, and reverse rollback | Lifecycle `deterministic-target-order-and-consumer-last` and `reverse-rollback-under-home-lock`; the latter requires reverse commit order, preimage checks, an unchanged unknown state, and the home lock through rollback. |
+| Concurrent projects and recovery | Lifecycle `two-project-success-preserves-both-consumers`, `successful-project-survives-other-project-rollback`, `interrupted-global-journal-recovered-by-transaction-id`, and `install-recovery-runs-after-private-builds`. |
+| Currentness, repair, and GC | Lifecycle `compiled-installation-current`, `compiled-currentness-failure-matrix`, `repair-rebuilds-invalid-compiled-entry`, `locked-mark-and-sweep-compiled-cache`, and `post-commit-gc-failure-is-maintenance-warning`. |
+| Fail-closed inventory/release evidence | Validator tests reject removed schemas/cases, unresolved references, stale hashes, and renamed lifecycle cases. Release-gate tests reject each missing required artifact, renamed v6 schemas, stale vector digests, missing manifest entries, removed cases, claim-version drift, rc.3 suite identity, and duplicate claim identity. |
+
+## Safety and publication boundary
+
+- All 75 build-driver rejection cases specify `artifact_executed: false` and
+  `reuse: false`.
+- The generator and validator do not invoke the package fixture or a compiled
+  package artifact. The accepted driver vector explicitly records no shell and
+  no artifact execution.
+- No implementation pin, tag, signature, checksum archive, attestation,
+  downstream manager release, or conformance claim was created. `RELEASE.md`
+  keeps external evidence prerequisites unchecked.
